[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61986,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Luteinized thecoma associated with sclerosing peritonitis is a distinctive ovarian stromal tumour typically associated with sclerosing peritonitis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61987,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8601/0 Thecoma, luteinized</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61988,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F32.Y &amp; XH0Z30 Other specified benign neoplasm of ovary &amp; Thecoma, luteinized</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61989,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> luteinized thecomatosis associated with sclerosing peritonitis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61990,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61991,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are localized in the ovary; when small, they may be confined to the ovarian cortex.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61992,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Luteinized thecoma associated with sclerosing peritonitis is almost always bilateral, and the usual presentation is with abdominal swelling, ascites, and symptoms of bowel obstruction. These symptoms are secondary to sclerosing peritonitis, which is nearly universal but may be subclinical and subtle. Hormonal manifestations are usually absent {18636018; 8279621}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61993,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is an extremely rare lesion. It most commonly occurs in young women (median age: 28&nbsp;years) {18636018}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61994,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61995,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The bilaterality, predominant cortical involvement, and envelopment of pre-existing ovarian structures suggest a non-neoplastic process in at least some cases {18636018}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61996,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Both ovaries are usually involved, although the degree of ovarian enlargement varies. The enlarged ovaries are usually soft and sometimes cerebriform, with a tan to red sectioned surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61997,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The ovaries are hypercellular, usually with scattered, often conspicuous zones of oedema, sometimes imparting a microcystic appearance. The cells are predominantly spindled, often with brisk mitotic activity. A minority of the cells are rounded, with pale or eosinophilic cytoplasm, representing luteinized or weakly luteinized cells. Entrapment of ovarian follicles and diffuse involvement of the cortex with sparing of the medulla may be conspicuous, especially when the ovaries are only mildly enlarged. The spindle cells are usually negative for inhibin and calretinin but positive for SF1 and FOXL2, whereas the luteinized cells are positive for inhibin and calretinin {18636018; 24076780}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61998,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 61999,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62000,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> cellular spindle cell proliferation with luteinized or weakly luteinized cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62001,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62002,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 70,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Several patients have died of complications related to intestinal obstruction due to the sclerosing peritonitis, but there has been no recurrence or metastasis of the ovarian lesion {18636018}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-13T17:04:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]